/* WIDER FLEET — one control in the technology row.

   Generation 202609030009 put twenty REPD technology types into #tech as
   twenty more buttons. Counted on that cut, nine of the twenty carry five
   rows or fewer, and the row held twenty-five controls: on a 390px phone the
   spine's own SOLAR / BATTERY / ONSHORE / OFFSHORE were pushed several
   wrapped lines down by tabs holding one and two projects each. This is the
   label and the select that replaced them.

   The 44px floor is set at EVERY width, not only under the phone breakpoint
   where 202608272048 already sets it for `select`. This control is the only
   way into twenty of the register's twenty-four technology types, and a 33px
   target is not made acceptable by a wide window. gridatlas v9.88 set that
   floor for this estate.

   min-width:0 is load-bearing, not tidiness. The phone block in
   202608270055-v8-fast.css sets `select { width:100%; min-width:100% }`, and
   100% of the flex parent plus a label plus a gap is wider than the row —
   which is the horizontal overflow this change exists to remove. A class
   beats a bare element selector, so these win regardless of sheet order. */

.wider-fleet-control {
  align-items: center;
  display: inline-flex;
  gap: 8px;
  max-width: 100%;
  min-width: 0;
}

.wider-fleet-label {
  color: #7f8996;
  font: 700 10px 'Courier New', monospace;
  letter-spacing: 1px;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.wider-fleet-select {
  max-width: 100%;
  min-height: 44px;
  min-width: 0;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  width: 22em;
}

.wider-fleet-select:hover,
.wider-fleet-select:focus {
  border-color: var(--accent);
  color: var(--accent);
}

/* Chosen: the control carries the mark the tab used to carry, so a reader can
   see at a glance that the table below is the wider fleet and not the product.
   The spine's own .btn.active is `color:#fff; border-color:#fff`. */
.wider-fleet-select.is-chosen {
  border-color: #fff;
  color: #fff;
}

.wider-fleet-control:has(.is-chosen) .wider-fleet-label {
  color: var(--accent);
}

@media (max-width: 768px), (orientation: landscape) and (max-height: 500px) and (min-width: 769px) {
  .wider-fleet-control {
    display: flex;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .wider-fleet-select {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    width: auto;
  }
}
